In triangle \(ABC\), we can use the angle bisector theorem and the formula for the length of the angle bisector. The length of the angle bisector \(CD\) in triangle \(ABC\) can be calculated using the formula: \[
CD = \sqrt{AB \cdot BC \left(1 - \frac{AC^2}{(AB + BC)^2}\right)}
